From: WordPress Playground contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Skip session file UID checks on WASI

WASI Preview 2 filesystems are capability based and do not expose a Unix user
identity model. wasi-libc consequently has no getuid() or geteuid(), so PHP's
Unix session-file ownership check cannot be compiled for this target.

The component host already limits session files to explicitly preopened
directories, and the native Playground host provides a private writable /tmp.
Keep the ownership check on Unix hosts and rely on those capability and host
filesystem boundaries for WASI.
---
 ext/session/mod_files.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ext/session/mod_files.c b/ext/session/mod_files.c
--- a/ext/session/mod_files.c
+++ b/ext/session/mod_files.c
@@ -190,7 +190,7 @@ static void ps_files_open(ps_files *data, /* const */ zend_string *key)
 #endif
 
 		if (data->fd != -1) {
-#ifndef PHP_WIN32
+#if !defined(PHP_WIN32) && !defined(PHP_WASI)
 			/* check that this session file was created by us or root – we
 			   don't want to end up accepting the sessions of another webapp
 
